\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces The two primary sources of error in this study, excluding errors originating from the sensors used: a) Wheat canopy's anisotropic BRDF, making the sun-sensor-field geometry relevant to the calculated GRVI value and b) The effect of shadows. These factors introduce noise to the perceived material reflectances, and therefore GRVI. Machine learning will be used for approximating the GRVI value under ideal illumination conditions, given the values measured under non-ideal conditions.}}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{ml-pipeline-1}{{1.1}{4}{The two primary sources of error in this study, excluding errors originating from the sensors used: a) Wheat canopy's anisotropic BRDF, making the sun-sensor-field geometry relevant to the calculated GRVI value and b) The effect of shadows. These factors introduce noise to the perceived material reflectances, and therefore GRVI. Machine learning will be used for approximating the GRVI value under ideal illumination conditions, given the values measured under non-ideal conditions}{figure.caption.6}{}}
